{"ts":"2026-05-18T15:00:00Z","source":"targets/coolblue-intigriti/opus/12.json + chains/_fp_archive.jsonl (entries 12,33,56,57,78)","kind":"teach-me-fp","pages_created":["wiki/techniques/recon/scope-aware-chain-triage.md","wiki/targets/coolblue-intigriti.md"],"pages_touched":[],"cross_links_added":3,"lesson":"Static taint pipeline harvests CDN assets linked from in-scope pages; chains with sinks on those out-of-scope hosts are unconfirmable. Pre-filter chains by sink_file host membership in http.md scope.in[] before audit spend, or route to _fp_archive in cc-taint-route. Browser-confirm must enforce as final guard."}
{"ts":"2026-05-18T15:35:00Z","source":"targets/coolblue-intigriti/findings/12/confirmed.json (chain 12 live-confirm result)","kind":"teach-me-fp-update","pages_touched":["wiki/techniques/recon/scope-aware-chain-triage.md","wiki/targets/coolblue-intigriti.md"],"pages_created":[],"cross_links_added":2,"lesson":"Distinguish execution origin from file host when scoping client-side chains. JS loaded from out-of-scope CDN via <script src=> in an in-scope page executes in the in-scope origin — XSS in that file is XSS on the in-scope app. Earlier 15:00 ingest framed file-host as scope filter; corrected after live-confirm of chain 12 showed the chain was reachable and in-scope but FP at gate 3 (endpoint /dist/preview_data.js returns 403, not deployed). Additional lesson: order live-probe gates by cost — gate 3 (cheap HTTP HEAD) kills chains in 1 round-trip before crafting state-flip payloads."}
{"ts":"2026-05-18T16:00:00Z","source":"targets/netlify-h1/findings/35589/confirmed.json (20-chain hot.jsonl batch FP)","kind":"teach-me-fp+pipeline-fix","pages_created":["wiki/techniques/recon/beautify-before-index.md","wiki/targets/netlify-h1.md"],"pages_touched":[],"cross_links_added":4,"lesson":"Beautify is a required phase before js-index on any target with minified bundles. Without it, function-boundary detection collapses, all chains report line=1 with mangled qnames, and chain extraction produces depth=0 self-flow noise (source.qname==sink.qname). Coolblue ran beautify, netlify-h1 did not — 20/20 hot chains were self-flow FPs as a direct consequence. Pipeline fix recipe documented; recommended target-init gate based on bytes/lines ratio."}
{"ts":"2026-05-18T16:35:00Z","source":"targets/netlify-h1/{beautify+reindex+chain_188 live-confirm}","kind":"pipeline-fix+chain-confirm","pages_created":["wiki/techniques/recon/initscript-pre-load-injection.md"],"pages_touched":["wiki/targets/netlify-h1.md"],"cross_links_added":3,"lesson":"Two lessons. (1) chrome-devtools MCP initScript injection captures page-load-time sinks that claude-in-chrome javascript_tool misses (post-navigate window globals wiped). Use chrome-devtools for any DOM-XSS chain that fires during bundle bootstrap. (2) Chain 188 (URLSearchParams_ctor → innerHTML_assign post-beautify) confirmed FP on unauth routes — URL params land only in URL-encoded href + sandboxed Stripe iframe. Authenticated routes still untested."}
{"ts":"2026-05-18T17:00:00Z","source":"targets/netlify-h1/findings/auth_dashboard_xss_sweep/confirmed.json","kind":"auth-dashboard-xss-sweep","pages_touched":["wiki/targets/netlify-h1.md"],"pages_created":[],"cross_links_added":1,"lesson":"Authenticated Netlify dashboard React app is XSS-clean across all probed user-controlled fields (OAuth app name/description/redirect URI; PAT description) and URL/hash sources on tested routes. All canaries land in text nodes via React JSX createTextNode — zero payload executions across 3 onload/onerror trip-wires. Consent screen also clean. GraphiQL bundle ships but no accessible mount as regular user. Untested: integrations, audit log, deploy detail, admin routes."}
{"ts":"2026-05-18T17:30:00Z","source":"2026-05-18 live-DOM sessions (coolblue chain 12 + netlify chain 188 + netlify auth sweep)","kind":"pattern-catalog+taxonomy-expansion","pages_created":["wiki/techniques/recon/live-dom-instrumentation-patterns.md"],"pages_touched":["tlx/modules/js_analyzer/taxonomies/extra_sinks.json","tlx/modules/js_analyzer/taxonomies/extra_sources.json"],"taxonomy_added":{"sinks":6,"sources":7},"taxonomy_total":{"sinks":51,"sources":41},"lesson":"7 reusable patterns from 3 live-DOM probe sessions: 3rd-party CDN dominates sink fires; React JSX text-node rendering is universally XSS-safe; SPA history.pushState makes hash chains dead; URL params on auth routes land in safe contexts; cross-frame postMessages are origin-gated; localStorage JWT = XSS severity escalator; unbeautified bundles produce self-flow noise. Per-chain-class live-probe recipes documented. Taxonomy extended with 6 sinks (script_src_setter, setAttribute_event_handler, dangerouslySetInnerHTML_prop, documentElement_innerHTML, iframe_src_url_hash, createElement_script_dynamic) and 7 sources (URLSearchParams_get_method, URL_searchParams_get_property, history_state_read, postMessage_event_origin, clipboard_paste_data, dataTransfer_getData, localStorage_jwt_pattern)."}
